WEBVTT

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:19.490
<i>The months that pass within my dreams</i>

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:23.410
<i>I cast aside my worldly desires 
along with my black hair</i>

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:29.670
<i>If I turn around, the stories of the 
past would appear before my eyes</i>

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:35.130
<i>In a drunken haze, I laugh at the world</i>

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:39.010
<i>Shangri-la is nowhere to be found</i>

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:44.810
<i>No one knows the love of the spring wind</i>

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:54.030
<i>The beginning and the 
end repeat over and over</i>

00:00:54.610 --> 00:01:01.990
<i>Trading places, they bloom then wilt</i>

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:05.830
<i>In January, I pick a flower with no petals</i>

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:13.170
<i>In February, I pick a flower 
that just started blooming</i>

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:17.680
<i>In March, the peach blossoms bloom</i>

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:24.640
<i>In April, the wisteria are in 
full bloom above the trellis</i>

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:28.690
<i>In February, I pick a flower 
that just started blooming</i>

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:32.780
<i>In April, the wisteria are in 
full bloom above the trellis</i>

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:42.740
<b>24:                Beijing</b>

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:59.670
<b><i>Hitorinoshita -The Outcast</i> comic is now being published in Shonen JUMP+!</b>

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:52.310
These are all of Den Shinchuu's memories.

00:01:52.310 --> 00:01:54.640
Well, Ro Ryou?

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:58.130
Was the brat really right?

00:01:58.930 --> 00:02:00.070
Probably.

00:02:00.790 --> 00:02:03.710
I haven't finished deciphering 
his memories yet,

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:09.370
but like the master suspected, Den Shinchuu 
knows something about the Koushin War.

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:15.530
Ah. This should make what 
happened then clear.

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:24.100
Why did our previous master 
Mukonsei betray us?

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:29.590
All of us approved of him.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:36.510
Ryuusei, don't let anyone know 
about Den Shinchuu's memories.

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:38.230
I know.

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:41.590
Not bad, kid.

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:42.910
Okay.

00:02:42.910 --> 00:02:45.510
You win this time.

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:51.960
As promised, we'll give you a 
second chance to order us around.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:56.000
You won't have to risk your life this time.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:03:01.010
In that case, as acting Master of 
Zensei, I issue the following order

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:03.200
to be carried out immediately.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:03.980
What?

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:10.920
Hold on. We just fought the Tenshifu.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:12.770
You want us to act again?

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:17.500
You must know how many casualties 
we suffered this time.

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:21.990
Tell all members that 
Grandmaster Den is dead.

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:23.940
We'll mourn for seven days.

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:26.360
Will that result in any casualties?

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.070
That's your order?

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:35.300
If anyone refuses, kill them for me.

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:36.780
That's all.

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:39.460
What a pain.

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:41.170
What should we do, Gramps?

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:45.230
The master's orders must be followed.

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:46.070
Huh?

00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:53.070
If you refuse his order,
I wouldn't mind killing you.

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:56.230
Fine.

00:03:56.230 --> 00:03:59.910
We just have to lay low for a week, right?

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:01.530
One more thing.

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:06.970
It will take time to decipher 
the stolen memories.

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:12.100
Don't cause any trouble for a while.

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:15.690
I can't have anyone interfering.

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:27.110
Master Den...

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:33.860
Eizan.

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:37.390
Everyone has their destiny.

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:40.690
There's nothing we can do.

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:46.050
Stand up, Eizan.

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:49.260
Eizan.

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:51.130
Eizan!

00:05:26.890 --> 00:05:28.090
Chou So—

00:05:27.230 --> 00:05:28.090
Houhou.

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:31.590
Don't say a word.

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:34.730
Leave them be.

00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:47.390
What?

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:49.030
Last night?

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:51.270
The Tenshifu was attacked?

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:58.460
I see. I'm glad I descended 
the mountain early.

00:06:01.810 --> 00:06:03.330
Yes, Master.

00:06:03.330 --> 00:06:06.760
Oh, right. I can't call you "master" anymore.

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:09.770
I've been expelled from Butousan.

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:14.220
<b>Butousan</b>

00:06:10.270 --> 00:06:14.240
I'll talk to the grandmaster about it.

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:17.080
In any case, come home.

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:19.630
Are you listening, Ouya?

00:06:20.930 --> 00:06:23.080
Unbelievable.

00:06:24.430 --> 00:06:26.160
Excuse me, Grandmaster.

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:30.580
Ah, Unryuu. What is it?

00:06:30.830 --> 00:06:34.210
Sir, why did you expel Ouya?

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:36.510
He's my apprentice.

00:06:36.510 --> 00:06:40.090
Shouldn't you have spoken with me first?

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:45.190
So much fuss over something so trivial.

00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:52.220
Unryuu, why did we send Ouya to Ryuukosan?

00:06:53.630 --> 00:07:01.010
To represent Butousan at the Raten 
Taishou and assist the Tenshi.

00:07:01.010 --> 00:07:03.190
That's right.

00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:11.530
So did he learn the technique he used 
to beat the Shokatsu boy from you?

00:07:12.390 --> 00:07:14.240
No, sir.

00:07:14.840 --> 00:07:17.900
Is it a Butousan technique?

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:24.880
No. Did you expel him for using 
another school's technique?

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:28.420
We should at least call him back and 
let him explain himself before—

00:07:31.690 --> 00:07:35.220
I am the master of Butousan.

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:37.730
Stay out of this.

00:07:39.490 --> 00:07:44.070
Remember this: Ouya and Butousan 
no longer have any connection.

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:51.850
If you still wish to be his 
master, then leave Butousan.

00:07:52.380 --> 00:07:54.270
Grandmaster, it's an emergency!

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:57.290
Grandmaster Ro has awoken!

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:04.260
Unryuu, this is no time to 
be worrying about Ouya.

00:08:05.470 --> 00:08:08.730
Things are no longer peaceful at Butousan.

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:12.750
Every night, someone tries to sneak in.

00:08:14.600 --> 00:08:20.070
Keep watch on them with the others.

00:08:20.690 --> 00:08:26.040
As long as they don't 
attack, leave them alone.

00:08:26.570 --> 00:08:31.180
Grandmaster, is this related to Ouya?

00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:34.850
That's none of your business.

00:08:40.360 --> 00:08:43.660
The beginning brings about the end.

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:48.960
The end changes, and I become king.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:51.990
The beginning brings about the end.

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:56.890
The end changes, and I become king.

00:08:57.340 --> 00:09:00.420
The beginning brings about the end.

00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:03.030
Ro Shikei.

00:09:04.590 --> 00:09:07.650
<i>We will be arriving in Beijing shortly.</i>

00:09:08.450 --> 00:09:11.750
<i>Please check your surroundings 
for any personal belongings.</i>

00:09:47.670 --> 00:09:50.030
What was that? A power outage?

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:53.620
Where did he go?

00:09:56.630 --> 00:09:59.980
I was wondering when they'd attack.

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:04.930
They probably expected me to let my 
guard down since I'd be home soon.

00:10:04.930 --> 00:10:06.900
Too bad.

00:10:23.960 --> 00:10:26.730
It's been a while, Young Master Ouya.

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:29.580
Don't call me that.

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:31.320
How many times do I have to tell you?

00:10:31.670 --> 00:10:33.720
Instructor Ouya, then?

00:10:33.720 --> 00:10:36.820
Enough. Thanks for the ride.

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:39.980
I heard the rumors.

00:10:39.980 --> 00:10:43.280
You've been expelled from Butousan.

00:10:43.780 --> 00:10:47.820
Now you're forced to work 
at your father's company.

00:10:47.820 --> 00:10:49.190
You're kidding.

00:10:49.190 --> 00:10:50.950
Word's already spread?

00:10:51.300 --> 00:10:53.750
Does my dad know?

00:10:53.750 --> 00:10:56.290
Of course the president knows.

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:59.120
You should hurry home.

00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:01.830
He's not doing well.

00:11:04.260 --> 00:11:06.850
<b>Beijing</b>

00:11:24.900 --> 00:11:26.820
<i>What is she doing?</i>

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:32.240
<i>She hasn't said a word to me since 
we returned from Ryuukosan.</i>

00:11:32.720 --> 00:11:35.210
<i>She's getting even worse.</i>

00:11:36.080 --> 00:11:38.550
<i>I can't take this anymore.</i>

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:43.360
Um, Hou-nee?

00:11:48.170 --> 00:11:50.990
Okay, okay! I'll tell you!

00:11:50.990 --> 00:11:53.560
I'll tell you everything
I discussed with the Tenshi!

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:55.920
Put that thing down!

00:11:57.280 --> 00:12:00.590
Jo San told me not to talk to you.

00:12:01.010 --> 00:12:02.660
That's what I've been doing.

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:03.190
Huh?

00:12:04.020 --> 00:12:05.890
You're sad, aren't you?

00:12:06.720 --> 00:12:07.520
Why?

00:12:10.550 --> 00:12:14.190
It's sad when family dies.

00:12:16.080 --> 00:12:19.590
It's sad when the person you love dies.

00:12:20.750 --> 00:12:25.930
That old man isn't your 
family, so why are you sad?

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:29.000
Do you love him?

00:12:29.730 --> 00:12:32.940
How can you love someone you only met once?

00:12:34.300 --> 00:12:35.530
Hou-nee...

00:12:37.850 --> 00:12:40.680
I decided not to become the Tenshi.

00:12:41.910 --> 00:12:47.170
So he wouldn't tell me the truth 
about the Koushin War.

00:12:48.680 --> 00:12:49.610
I'm sorry.

00:13:04.770 --> 00:13:05.850
Hou-nee?

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:12.480
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:13:13.970 --> 00:13:17.070
<i>Ouya-san's warning and the 
Tenshi's words and actions</i>

00:13:17.070 --> 00:13:20.310
<i>indicated that trying to learn 
more about the Koushin War</i>

00:13:20.790 --> 00:13:23.120
<i>would bring about misfortune.</i>

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:30.410
<i>But I don't know how serious it would 
be, and it's all just conjecture.</i>

00:13:30.950 --> 00:13:34.450
<i>But there's no guarantee 
that learning the truth</i>

00:13:34.450 --> 00:13:37.690
<i>about the Koushin War will 
explain Hou-nee's past.</i>

00:13:38.470 --> 00:13:39.470
<i>In that case...</i>

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:42.330
Hou-nee.

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:47.530
Maybe you don't need to be 
bound by your past anymore.

00:13:48.570 --> 00:13:52.140
Maybe your family is still out there.

00:14:01.060 --> 00:14:02.230
Hou-nee!

00:14:03.450 --> 00:14:06.330
Hou-nee, stop this.

00:14:07.290 --> 00:14:10.340
You're not the only one who doesn't 
have a place to return to.

00:14:10.790 --> 00:14:12.780
I don't have any family, either.

00:14:15.220 --> 00:14:19.820
Hou-nee, I'll continue to stay by your side.

00:14:20.300 --> 00:14:24.430
Like Jo Shou-san, the man 
you used to be with.

00:14:24.770 --> 00:14:27.180
I'll do more than stay by your side.

00:14:27.180 --> 00:14:29.000
I'll do whatever you want.

00:14:29.390 --> 00:14:30.320
So—

00:14:30.320 --> 00:14:31.130
Liar.

00:14:31.130 --> 00:14:31.970
Huh?

00:14:32.750 --> 00:14:34.610
You have one.

00:14:36.840 --> 00:14:37.950
Here.

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:39.810
It's in here.

00:14:40.740 --> 00:14:45.460
You all have a place to return to in here.

00:15:00.130 --> 00:15:01.230
Hou-nee.

00:15:03.560 --> 00:15:04.570
I'm sorry.

00:15:05.080 --> 00:15:07.940
There's something I couldn't 
tell you earlier.

00:15:08.720 --> 00:15:11.010
<b>Jo Yon
Incoming Call</b>

00:15:12.080 --> 00:15:13.830
Can you hear me, Jo Yon?

00:15:13.830 --> 00:15:15.640
<i>Yeah, no problem.</i>

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:16.850
Good.

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:22.490
You guys all know I decided 
not to succeed the Tenshi.

00:15:23.080 --> 00:15:27.070
It may look like we gained 
nothing from this tournament,

00:15:27.760 --> 00:15:29.330
but that's not the case.

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:33.270
The reason we have that impression

00:15:33.620 --> 00:15:39.330
is because we've been misled since
Jo Shou-san watched my grandfather die.

00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:40.930
Misled?

00:15:41.600 --> 00:15:44.880
On his deathbed, my grandfather said...

00:15:46.060 --> 00:15:48.570
All of the secrets surrounding Fuu Houhou

00:15:48.570 --> 00:15:51.130
have to do with the Koushin War.

00:15:52.340 --> 00:15:54.690
Please protect Soran.

00:15:54.690 --> 00:15:59.780
Then you will be able to regain your past.

00:16:00.570 --> 00:16:02.110
The Koushin War.

00:16:02.620 --> 00:16:06.630
My grandfather made Jo Shou-san 
believe he'd learn Hou-nee's past

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:08.880
if he uncovered the truth about it.

00:16:09.690 --> 00:16:14.630
He claimed the key to learning the 
truth about the Koushin War was me.

00:16:15.330 --> 00:16:21.250
Which means Hou-nee would be forced to 
protect me until the truth was revealed.

00:16:23.130 --> 00:16:27.170
My grandfather must've thought there was 
no way for you to discover the truth.

00:16:27.950 --> 00:16:34.460
As long as you didn't, I'd have 
a powerful bodyguard in Hou-nee.

00:16:36.190 --> 00:16:40.150
My grandfather used Jo Shou-san and Hou-nee.

00:16:41.600 --> 00:16:44.480
So my father was deceived by Chou Kaigi.

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:47.750
<i>Chou Kaigi wasn't lying.</i>

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:52.570
<i>He just created a small pitfall in his story.</i>

00:16:52.870 --> 00:16:53.850
That's right.

00:16:53.850 --> 00:16:59.770
Like my grandfather said, Hou-nee's past 
must be related to the Koushin War.

00:17:00.550 --> 00:17:04.240
But it's not related to all of it.

00:17:05.380 --> 00:17:09.760
Remember our meeting with the Elders.

00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:14.150
The Tenshi, Shinchuu-sama, and Rikukin-sama...

00:17:14.150 --> 00:17:17.300
Their words and actions are a major clue.

00:17:18.200 --> 00:17:23.180
Shinchuu-sama and Rikukin-sama 
readily told us what they knew.

00:17:23.820 --> 00:17:27.830
But the Tenshi stubbornly 
kept his mouth shut.

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:30.420
Don't you think that means something?

00:17:31.050 --> 00:17:34.940
<i>So the Tenshi holds some key information.</i>

00:17:36.730 --> 00:17:42.110
The Tenshi said he'd tell 
me about the Koushin War

00:17:42.950 --> 00:17:45.590
if I agreed to become his successor.

00:17:46.950 --> 00:17:50.870
In other words, you can only learn 
the truth if you become the Tenshi.

00:17:51.530 --> 00:17:56.330
The truth must lie in the way of the Tenshi.

00:17:57.150 --> 00:18:01.030
Then shouldn't you have 
agreed to succeed him?

00:18:01.570 --> 00:18:06.350
If you became the Tenshi, you would've 
uncovered the truth about the Koushin War.

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:11.770
When I saw the light of the way of the 
Tenshi he was trying to teach me,

00:18:13.050 --> 00:18:16.850
I recalled my grandfather 
marking me with the seal.

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:23.150
Accepting the way of the Tenshi 
might have revealed the truth,

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:28.450
but I felt it would also 
suppress something inside me.

00:18:28.810 --> 00:18:34.710
I might have lost the ability to 
even discuss the Koushin War.

00:18:36.470 --> 00:18:38.980
Master, please tell me.

00:18:40.060 --> 00:18:41.930
I must know.

00:18:42.950 --> 00:18:47.750
Once you give me the way of the 
Tenshi, what will happen to you?

00:18:50.990 --> 00:18:54.600
Like grandfather, like grandson.

00:18:54.600 --> 00:18:57.620
You worry too much.

00:18:58.680 --> 00:19:05.200
In that moment, I became certain the Raten 
Taishou was held to tie me to the Tenshifu.

00:19:06.630 --> 00:19:10.490
That's why I refused to become 
the Tenshi's successor.

00:19:11.660 --> 00:19:15.780
The way of the Tenshi must be 
some kind of suppression spell.

00:19:16.270 --> 00:19:21.430
I'm not certain, but I think it's 
related to the eight secret arts.

00:19:23.720 --> 00:19:27.100
Eight members of the 36 families 
involved in the Koushin War

00:19:27.100 --> 00:19:30.620
created secret arts no ordinary 
person could conceive of.

00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:32.730
But how?

00:19:33.430 --> 00:19:38.510
<i>Even if a single genius miraculously 
created a secret art,</i>

00:19:38.510 --> 00:19:41.960
<i>it's unlikely that eight of 
them did it simultaneously.</i>

00:19:42.410 --> 00:19:43.220
That's right.

00:19:43.600 --> 00:19:46.570
Everyone must want to know that secret.

00:19:47.270 --> 00:19:52.140
And maybe that secret is 
in the way of the Tenshi.

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:58.410
No, it's possible the eight secret arts 
were created from the way of the Tenshi.

00:20:00.380 --> 00:20:03.380
That's bad news if it's true.

00:20:03.820 --> 00:20:06.850
There's no evidence.
It's just my conjecture.

00:20:07.360 --> 00:20:13.230
But if it's true, then we don't need 
to involve ourselves any further.

00:20:13.770 --> 00:20:18.780
Our goal is Hou-nee's past, not revealing 
the truth about the Koushin War.

00:20:21.840 --> 00:20:22.760
What is it?

00:20:24.170 --> 00:20:28.090
Hou-nee, this is just a hunch,

00:20:28.090 --> 00:20:32.430
but I don't think your past is 
related to the Koushin War.

00:20:34.330 --> 00:20:41.080
But the survivors of the war might 
know something about your past.

00:20:41.750 --> 00:20:45.530
Fortunately, we made a few connections 
during the Raten Taishou.

00:20:46.180 --> 00:20:50.810
You could say it's our biggest 
win at the Raten Taishou.

00:20:51.300 --> 00:20:55.340
Come to think of it, since 
I saved Riku Rinron,

00:20:55.340 --> 00:20:57.780
Rikukin-sama said he owes me a huge favor.

00:20:57.780 --> 00:20:59.740
We might be able to get 
something out of him.

00:21:00.730 --> 00:21:04.140
So just wait a little longer.

00:21:04.950 --> 00:21:08.830
I promise we'll find your family.

00:21:11.510 --> 00:21:12.710
I'll be waiting.

00:21:13.310 --> 00:21:17.610
Jo Yon, sometimes he's smarter than me.

00:21:17.610 --> 00:21:19.580
<i>Sometimes?</i>

00:21:20.210 --> 00:21:24.390
Soran-kun, we agree with your reasoning.

00:21:24.960 --> 00:21:29.470
But don't contact Rikukin-sama for a while.

00:21:30.080 --> 00:21:34.480
There's probably a lot to handle in 
the aftermath of the Raten Taishou.

00:21:35.020 --> 00:21:39.020
You've also received a 
mission from the office.

00:21:39.020 --> 00:21:40.580
